<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><id>https://howlcipher.github.io/bullpenphone/feeds/det.xml</id><title>Bullpen Phone: Detroit Tigers reporter posts</title><link rel="self" href="https://howlcipher.github.io/bullpenphone/feeds/det.xml"/><link href="https://howlcipher.github.io/bullpenphone/"/><updated>2026-11-07T13:34:48.860Z</updated><entry><id>https://howlcipher.github.io/bullpenphone/t/staff-det/#2026-11-06T16:12:39.899Z</id><title>Detroit Tigers staff and front office: Tigers finalize their coaching staff, formally announcing Kyle Hudson and Martin Maldonado as coaches. Catching coach Ryan Sienko will also serve as bullpen coach, filling an opening left when assistant pitching coach Juan Nieves was not retained.</title><link href="https://bsky.app/profile/jasonbeck.bsky.social/post/3mznrktt2vs22"/><link rel="related" href="https://howlcipher.github.io/bullpenphone/t/staff-det/"/><updated>2026-11-06T16:12:39.899Z</updated><summary>staff, reported by Jason Beck</summary><author><name>Jason Beck</name></author></entry><entry><id>https://howlcipher.github.io/bullpenphone/t/player-445276/#2026-11-02T23:21:56.362Z</id><title>Kenley Jansen: Tigers decline $12 million option on Kenley Jansen, he will hit free agency two saves shy of 500....other moves...</title><link href="https://bsky.app/profile/cmccosky.bsky.social/post/3mzehoravtc2r"/><link rel="related" href="https://howlcipher.github.io/bullpenphone/t/player-445276/"/><updated>2026-11-02T23:21:56.362Z</updated><summary>Unclassified, reported by Chris McCosky</summary><author><name>Chris McCosky</name></author></entry><entry><id>https://howlcipher.github.io/bullpenphone/t/team-det/#2026-11-02T22:52:51.353Z</id><title>Detroit Tigers offseason notes: Tigers moves: Kenley Jansen’s $12m option declined. He gets a $2m buyout. Drew Anderson’s $10m option picked up. Jacob Waguespack re-signed to a 1-yr, $1.3m MLB contract with another $200k in bonuses based on innings pitched.</title><link href="https://bsky.app/profile/jasonbeck.bsky.social/post/3mzeg2r3jgk23"/><link rel="related" href="https://howlcipher.github.io/bullpenphone/t/team-det/"/><updated>2026-11-02T22:52:51.353Z</updated><summary>team, reported by Jason Beck</summary><author><name>Jason Beck</name></author></entry><entry><id>https://howlcipher.github.io/bullpenphone/t/player-691907/#2026-10-30T12:20:22.599Z</id><title>Tsung-Che Cheng: Confirming Masslive report, Tigers have acquired left-handed hitting middle infielder Tsung-Che Cheng from Boston for cash</title><link href="https://bsky.app/profile/cmccosky.bsky.social/post/3mz3rczx6es26"/><link rel="related" href="https://howlcipher.github.io/bullpenphone/t/player-691907/"/><updated>2026-10-30T12:20:22.599Z</updated><summary>Unclassified, reported by Chris McCosky</summary><author><name>Chris McCosky</name></author></entry><entry><id>https://howlcipher.github.io/bullpenphone/t/player-675512/#2026-10-15T14:05:40.936Z</id><title>Troy Melton: Tigers released some good news regarding Troy Melton. He’s been cleared medically, no damage to his arm, and will have a normal offseason</title><link href="https://bsky.app/profile/cmccosky.bsky.social/post/3mxwa7jobe223"/><link rel="related" href="https://howlcipher.github.io/bullpenphone/t/player-675512/"/><updated>2026-10-15T14:05:40.936Z</updated><summary>Unclassified, reported by Chris McCosky</summary><author><name>Chris McCosky</name></author></entry></feed>